WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.058
(uptempo music)

00:00:01.058 --> 00:00:04.464
- [Narrator] There are 43
quintillion possible combinations.

00:00:04.464 --> 00:00:06.911
Now imagine you have no websites, no books

00:00:06.911 --> 00:00:08.992
and no one to show you how to solve it,

00:00:08.992 --> 00:00:10.992
because you invented it.

00:00:12.599 --> 00:00:15.090
But you didn't invent the Rubik's Cube.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:15.923
(enchanting music)

00:00:15.923 --> 00:00:17.006
This guy did.

00:00:24.554 --> 00:00:26.260
It was 1974.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.423
Thirty-year-old Erno Rubik was just beginning

00:00:28.423 --> 00:00:30.340
his career in academia.

00:00:50.032 --> 00:00:52.162
Once the physical cube was put together,

00:00:52.162 --> 00:00:55.079
Erno began hunting for its secrets.

00:01:12.379 --> 00:01:14.779
Erno racked his brain for a strategy,

00:01:14.779 --> 00:01:16.570
twisting and turning the cube in his hands

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.570
and his head to unlock his creation.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:31.887
And after a month, he cracked the code.

00:01:31.887 --> 00:01:33.838
(turning cube)

00:01:33.838 --> 00:01:36.505
But the story doesn't end there.

00:01:47.513 --> 00:01:49.734
In 1980, Erno would finally bring his cube

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:50.902
to the world.

00:01:50.902 --> 00:01:52.502
And from there, it took off,

00:01:52.502 --> 00:01:54.077
becoming one of the best selling toys

00:01:54.077 --> 00:01:55.077
of all time.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.401
And after almost 40 years,

00:02:06.401 --> 00:02:08.390
Rubik's Cube has seen a comeback,

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.166
with hundreds of competitions every year

00:02:10.166 --> 00:02:11.583
across the world.

00:02:13.006 --> 00:02:15.238
For Erno, the cube that bears his name

00:02:15.238 --> 00:02:17.262
is more than just a toy:

00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:20.012
it's a reminder to never give up.

